    "https://www.carthage.edu/why-carthage/career-preparation/": {
      "title": "Career Preparation & Internships",
      "description": "Career Preparation & Internships • Why Carthage • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Career Preparation & Internships Home Why Carthage Career Preparation & Internships Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View ENTRANCE RAMP TO SUCCESS Built exclusively for Carthage students, The Aspire Program connects interests to hidden career paths as you grow into a versatile professional who’s equipped to handle anything. All students participate, and we spread the tasks across four years so it won’t stress you out. Think of it as a guided pathway to a great job and, even better, a rewarding life. Shape Your Future Entering The Aspire Program, students start shaping a customized career plan in their first days on campus. Here are a few of the highlights: Make Connections Based on your interests, we’ll match you with a career specialist who knows the industry inside and out. Plus, it’s easy to network with Carthage graduates working in similar fields. You can even attend a professional conference without leaving campus. Learn by Doing Valuable hands-on experience can give you an early edge in the competitive job market. Internships: Our prime location between Milwaukee and Chicago puts internships with all kinds of companies and organizations within reach. If you find a great opportunity that just doesn’t pay enough, Carthage has funding available. Study Abroad: Whether they learn overseas for a year, a semester, or just a few weeks through our popular J-Term study tours, students consistently return transformed. Research: Here, original research is part of every student’s journey. Faculty in the sciences lead experiments with big-time partners like NASA, but all majors require a scholarly project to graduate. Internships provide hands-on learning at companies like Snap-On, Jockey, Abbott Laboratories, Fiserv Forum, and more! Carthage space science students have interned at the NASA Kennedy Space Center and at the NASA Academy at NASA Langley Research Center. It’s not just about getting a great job. The Aspire Program is about understanding how your activities in and outside of work can help you to build a satisfying life. Early and often in their time at Carthage, students are challenged to perform original study under the close guidance of experienced faculty. Carthage hosts several events throughout the year, including career fairs and networking opportunities, so students can learn more about available internship, grad school, and career prep opportunities. › Previous slide › Next slide MORE ABOUT THE ASPIRE PROGRAM “The Aspire Program has been a helpful resource in preparing me for a career. The staff have supported me with resume reviews, career advice, and guidance on professional development.” — Ryan Fuentes ’28 Gain opportunities through Carthage professors Thanks to Carthage’s small class sizes, students build strong connections with professors who actively support them in landing internships and jobs. Meet Carthage professors who help students land jobs Start Exploring Explore Majors And Careers Have A Plan From Day One Why Carthage? Exploration & Mentorship 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Opportunities Abroad 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/life-at-carthage/aspire/": {
      "title": "The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development",
      "description": "The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development Home The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development Career Preparation starting Day One The Aspire Program at Carthage is a multifaceted four-year career development sequence designed exclusively for Carthage students. Identify your interests and purpose and connect the dots to potential careers. The program prepares you for a meaningful life, no matter what the future holds. The Four-Year Plan <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg\" alt=\"Makenzie Baker '27\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"2316\" data-max-h=\"2316\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “I used The Aspire Program during my freshman year. My advisor helped me set up my resume and start building my experience.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3396-makenzie-baker\">Makenzie Baker</a> ’27</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg\" alt=\"Anita Gross '28\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"2130\" data-max-h=\"2130\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program staff have helped me build an academic resume that looks professional and even taught me how to search for internships on LinkedIn.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3413-anita-gross\">Anita Gross</a> ’28</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg\" alt=\"Ryan Fuentes '28\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1251\" data-max-h=\"1250\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program has been a helpful resource in preparing me for a career. The staff have supported me with resume reviews, career advice, and guidance on professional development.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3411-ryan-fuentes\">Ryan Fuentes</a> ’28</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg\" alt=\"Joey Westphal '27\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1837\" data-max-h=\"1837\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program staff helped me create my resume, look for internships, and practice in mock interviews.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3412-joey-westphal\">Joey Westphal</a> ’27</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg\" alt=\"Kelvin Madjinor '27\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"570\" data-max-h=\"569\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “With the help of The Aspire Program staff, I’ve created a resume and gained connections with alumni.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3008-kelvin-madjinor\">Kelvin Madjinor</a> ’27</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg\" alt=\"Evan Reinemann '28\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1068\" data-max-h=\"1069\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program has played an important role in preparing me for my career by offering resources such as job search assistance, resume building, and free professional headshots.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3556-evan-reinemann\">Evan Reinemann</a> ’28</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> About The Aspire Program At Carthage, all first-year students begin career development planning from their first days on campus. Through The Aspire Program, they develop a dynamic approach to goal-setting and life skill-building. Students will own their ability to be lifelong learners and impactful contributors in the world, and to recover when plans don’t go as expected. Launched in 2019, The Aspire Program builds on Carthage’s strong history of providing students with the skills they need to succeed. For Carthage Students Stories & Outcomes Employers & Community View {title} video embed Learn more about Carthage’s Aspire Program. Close YouTube Video: {title} Enable Javascript to view the video embed or view the video directly at https://youtube.com/watch?v=EGkcFp6359Q . Driving Student Success The Aspire Program at Carthage College is nationally recognized for its innovative approach to career development. With numerous awards, competitive grant support, and featured case studies, the program continues to lead in student success. See the Aspire Program’s Awards Hear from our employer partners “Partnering with Carthage College and The Aspire Program has been an incredibly rewarding experience. Their commitment to preparing students for life beyond the classroom is truly inspiring. The Aspire Program’s team is collaborative, responsive, and clearly passionate about creating meaningful connections between students and the professional world. I’ve been continually impressed by their innovative approach and the value they bring to both students and external partners.\" — Dulce Morales, Senior Lead, Community Relations and Business Development at BCU “Abbott Finance, Carthage College, and The Aspire Program have built a great relationship over the past few years. Abbott has been allowed to engage with students each year and present on career opportunities. In doing so, we’ve been able to recruit bright and driven talent from Carthage into our co-op/internship program and as full-time employees. We hope to continue to build upon this relationship in the future.” — Asif Choudhury, Sr. Finance Manager at Abbott “Carthage College is a distinguished institution for education, personal development, and career preparation. The collaboration between The Aspire Program and the Kenosha Police Department has thrived. We appreciate the dedication of Carthage interns at our department and their commitment to our city and organization. We are grateful for this partnership and eagerly anticipate offering more programs to strengthen our community together.” — Jason Tetrick, Lieutenant and Training Officer at Kenosha Police Department › Previous slide › Next slide Connect with Us Aspire Staff Find Your Career Specialist Handshake and Other Resources News from the Aspire Program News & Events 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/careers-at-carthage/": {
      "title": "Careers",
