    "https://www.carthage.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/careers-at-carthage/faculty-positions/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Carthage: Faculty Positions • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Careers at Carthage: Faculty Positions Home Human Resources Careers at Carthage Faculty Positions Offices & Services Human Resources New Employees Current Employees Careers at Carthage Faculty Positions Staff Positions Current Openings: Faculty Positions Assistant Professor of Nursing (Mental Health) The Faculty of Nursing at Carthage College is responsible for didactic and clinical teaching in the department’s nursing programs, maintaining competence in an area of nursing practice, and providing service to the College and the community. Read More “Assistant Professor of Nursing (Mental Health)” Adjunct Assistant Professor, History Carthage College Department of History (www.carthage.edu/history) invites applications for part-time instructors to teach an introductory course in American History, any period, any specialization. The course will be taught in Spring 2026, with the possibility of teaching in the following year. Read More “Adjunct Assistant Professor, History” Adjunct Assistant Professor, Biology The Biology Department invites applications for part-time adjunct instructors to teach a variety of courses for majors and non-majors. Read More “Adjunct Assistant Professor, Biology” Adjunct Assistant Professor, Nursing The Nursing Department at Carthage College invites applications for an Adjunct Assistant Professor of Nursing position starting August 15, 2026. Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until positions are filled. Read More “Adjunct Assistant Professor, Nursing” Assistant Professor, Biology The Biology Department at Carthage College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biology position in Biology with a focus on Cell Biology starting August 15, 2027 or possibly January 15, 2027. For best consideration for applications should be received by October 1, 2026. Read More “Assistant Professor, Biology” Adjunct Assistant Professor, Art and Design The Carthage College Art & Design Department is currently accepting applications for an Adjunct Professor of Film (Production). The position is for the 2026 fall semester and begins August 26 and ends Dec 11. Read More “Adjunct Assistant Professor, Art and Design” Visiting Assistant Professor, Mathematics The Mathematics Department at Carthage College invites applicants for a two-year non-renewable position as Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2026. Read More “Visiting Assistant Professor, Mathematics” Adjunct Assistant Professor, Biochemistry The Department of Chemistry at Carthage College invites applications for a part-time laboratory teaching position for Spring 2027 (February–May). The instructor will teach one section of Biochemistry Laboratory. Read More “Adjunct Assistant Professor, Biochemistry” Adjunct Assistant Professors, Business & Economics The School of Business and Economics is seeking qualified candidates for a multiple adjunct positions starting Fall of 2025. The individuals may teach undergraduate and graduate courses in various areas such as Product Management, Design & Innovation, Marketing, Human Resource Management, Economics, Accounting and Finance. Read More “Adjunct Assistant Professors, Business & Economics” See Current Openings: Staff Positions 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/careers-at-carthage/staff-positions/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Carthage: Staff Positions • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Careers at Carthage: Staff Positions Home Human Resources Careers at Carthage Staff Positions Offices & Services Human Resources New Employees Current Employees Careers at Carthage Faculty Positions Staff Positions Current openings: Staff Positions EVS Technician Performs manual labor tasks and related work to clean and sanitize public buildings, offices, athletic facilities, and college resident halls. Serves as a dependable and flexible team member to support departmental objectives and meet productivity and quality standards. Read More “EVS Technician” Senior Grant & Gift Manager The Senior Grant & Gift Manager at Carthage College oversees the financial administration, accounting, compliance, reporting, and stewardship of restricted grants, gifts, endowments, pledges, and other donor-restricted funds. As the College’s subject matter expert for grant and gift accounting, this position ensures compliance with federal, state, sponsor, donor, and institutional requirements. Read More “Senior Grant & Gift Manager” Hall Director The Hall Director is an eleven-month, live-in professional staff member who works closely with other College personnel to address the social, developmental, and academic needs of our students. Read More “Hall Director” Nursing Clinical Placement Coordinator The Nursing Clinical Placement Coordinator is responsible for planning, organizing, and executing student clinical site placements and clinical rotations across undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. Read More “Nursing Clinical Placement Coordinator” Benefits Specialist The Benefits Specialist will be responsible for the administration of benefits programs with regards to plan options, features, enrollment, and other requirements. This strategic position will assure compliance and working directly with vendors to provide information that is related to navigating the benefits. This role will also support the activities necessary to process payroll. Read More “Benefits Specialist” School of Business & Economics (SOBE) Graduate Assistant Carthage College is seeking to fill one Graduate Assistant position for the 2026-2027 and 2027-2028 academic year. Read More “School of Business & Economics (SOBE) Graduate Assistant” Executive Director, Regional Employment The Executive Director will lead the implementation of a regional strategy designed to attract, retain, and connect young adults in a variety of life circumstances to economic opportunity in the Kenosha/Racine region. The position will transform a strategic vision into an operational system that integrates workforce development, community building, and talent attraction. Read More “Executive Director, Regional Employment” See Current Openings: Faculty Positions 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    }
